region : A Region is a geographical location in the cloud where data centers are located, and it is 
         isolated from other regions for fault tolerance and high availability.


availability zones: An Availability Zone is a single, isolated data center (or a group of closely located data centers) within a region.
local Zones: Local Zones are extensions of AWS regions that place compute, storage, and other services closer to end users.

wavwlength Zones: Wavelength Zones are AWS infrastructure deployments inside telecom (5G) networks to provide ultra-low latency.

